# L §3.2 Inline figures: "A bare 0, 1 or -1 takes the unit of the other operand in +, -, min, max and comparisons,
# is dimensionless in * and /, and takes the declared type of its target where it is a whole value".
# max(0, a - b) with a = 10.00, b = 30.00 PLN: max(0 PLN, -20.00 PLN) = 0.00 PLN; a * -1 = -10.00 PLN (money × int);
# a rule value 0 of a money def is 0.00 PLN.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
unit hour "godzina"

input a: money PLN
input b: money PLN

def d: money PLN at reader
  rule base = max(0, a - b)
def e: money PLN at reader
  rule base = a * -1
def z: money PLN at reader
  rule base = 0

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  a = 10.00 PLN
  b = 30.00 PLN

ask q1: d, e, z law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: (0.00 PLN, -10.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
